{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima and Lateralus feel like natural next choices after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's heavy, intricate, immersive music.",
    "Hypnotize fits the forceful riffs and unusual rhythms I am drawn to in my recent Tool and Disturbed listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Stadium Arcadium and Good News For People Who Love Bad News lean toward funkier or quirky indie rock, which does not satisfy my current interest in heavier music.",
    "Significant Other emphasizes rap rock, while the heaviness I want right now comes with progressive complexity or melodic metal."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in rock seems to have been treated too broadly, even though different rock sounds are not equally appealing to me today.",
    "Past interest in Chuck and The Reason makes punk and melodic rock relevant, but does not make them my first choices after my recent Tool listening."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest choice, 10.000 Days, makes another Tool album especially appealing right now.",
    "Aggression or complexity alone is not enough: St. Anger and Amputechture interest me, but Tool's combination of heaviness and intricate arrangements is what I most want today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy rock, but only some capture my current preference for Tool's immersive, intricate heaviness."
}"}
